# Execute with script nodes: a call inserts a script node and takes a screenshot of its frame, which shows the
# node's output once it has run (Finish runs it without the lock and redraws from the call's document); an export
# of it too; then a screenshot of the node that has run already. The node runs with an input and size no other
# sequence uses, in a document of its own: script runs and their slots are process-wide, and the Go replays share
# one process.
